ield(load_path=load_path, arrayName=\"pressure\")\n171:        field_view = EmbedScalarField(\n172-            parent_node_id=scalar.id,\n173-            colormap=\"viridis\",\n174-        )\n--\n238-    Loads a scalar field. load_path is a VTI or time-series directory. arrayName is\n239-    the point-data array; it may be empty only when the file has one array.\n240-\n241:LoadVectorField(load_path, u_array_name, v_array_name)\n242-    Loads a 2D vector field from the point arrays holding its x/u and y/v\n243-    components.\n244-\n--\n253-FIELD EMBEDDINGS\n254-----------------\n255-\n256:EmbedScalarField(parent_node_id, colormap=\"cool warm\")\n257-    Displays a scalar field as a colored surface (2D) or volume (3D). colormap must\n258-    be one of the colormap names listed in Section 2.\n259-\n260:EmbedVectorField(parent_node_id)\n261-    Displays a vector field using its geometric vector-field embedding.\n262-\n263:EmbedSymmetricTensorField(parent_node_id)\n264-    Displays a symmetric tensor field using its geometric tensor embedding.\n265-\n266:EmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvectorPartition(parent_node_id, resolution=16)\n267-    Displays the asymmetric-tensor domain partitioned by eigenvector behavior.\n268-    resolution is the number of subdivisions per grid cell; higher is slower and\n269-    smoother.\n270-\n271:EmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvaluePartition(parent_node_id, resolution=16)\n272-    Displays regions dominated by scaling, rotation, or anisotropic stretching,\n273-    including direction where applicable. resolution controls subdivisions per\n274-    grid cell.\n--\n284-ComputePersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id)\n285-    Computes a scalar field's persistence diagram.\n286-\n287:EmbedPersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id, ball_radius=0.02, tube_radius=0.01)\n288-    Displays persistence pairs as balls and tubes. Both radii are fractions of the\n289-    scalar function range.\n290-\n291-ComputeMorseSmaleSegmentation(parent_node_id)\n292-    Computes the Morse-Smale segmentation of a scalar field.\n293-\n294:EmbedMorseSmaleSegmentation(parent_node_id)\n295-    Creates displayable geometry for a Morse-Smale segmentation.\n296-\n297-ComputeIsocontours(parent_node_id, num_contours)\n298-    Computes num_contours isovalues uniformly across a scalar field's value range.\n299-\n300:EmbedIsocontours(parent_node_id, colormap=\"cool warm\", tube_radius=1.0)\n301-    Displays isocontours with the selected colormap. tube_radius is the contour tube\n302-    radius used for 2D data.\n303-\n304-ComputeContourTree(parent_node_id)\n305-    Computes a scalar field's contour tree.\n306-\n307:EmbedContourTree(parent_node_id, ball_radius=3.0, tube_radius=1.5,\n308-                 color_scheme=[\"#002fff\", \"#758fff\", \"#ffdee7\", \"#ff0046\",\n309-                               \"#000000\"])\n310-    Displays contour-tree vertices and edges. ball_radius and tube_radius size the\n--\n314-ComputeMergeTree(parent_node_id, which_tree=\"join\")\n315-    Computes a merge tree. which_tree must be \"join\" or \"split\".\n316-\n317:EmbedMergeTree(parent_node_id, ball_radius=3.0, tube_radius=1.5,\n318-               color_scheme=[\"#002fff\", \"#758fff\", \"#ffdee7\", \"#ff0046\",\n319-                             \"#000000\"])\n320-    Displays merge-tree vertices and edges. Parameters have the same meanings and\n321:    color order as EmbedContourTree.\n322-\n323-\n324-FIELD-TO-FIELD OPERATIONS\n325--------------------------\n326-\n327:VectorFieldMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n328-    Converts a vector field to a scalar magnitude field.\n329-\n330-SymmetricTensorMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n--\n336-ScalarGradient(parent_node_id)\n337-    Converts a scalar field to its vector gradient field.\n338-\n339:VectorGradient(parent_node_id)\n340-    Converts a vector field to its asymmetric-tensor gradient/Jacobian field.\n341-\n342-\n343-POINT COMPUTATION AND EMBEDDING\n344--------------------------------\n345-\n346:ComputeScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, which_points)\n347-    Computes selected critical points of a scalar field. which_points must be one\n348-    of these exact strings:\n349-      - \"all critical points (mins+maxes+saddles)\"\n--\n353-      - \"all contour tree vertices (mins+maxes+saddles)\"\n354-      - \"contour tree saddles\"\n355-\n356:ComputeVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id)\n357-    Computes critical points of a vector field.\n358-\n359-ComputeSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id)\n--\n362-ComputeAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id)\n363-    Computes degenerate points of an asymmetric tensor field.\n364-\n365:EmbedScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n366-                          color_scheme=[\"#3b4cc0\", \"#aac7fd\", \"#f7b89c\",\n367-                                        \"#b40426\", \"#000000\"])\n368-    Displays scalar critical points as spheres. radius controls sphere size.\n369-    color_scheme contains five hex colors for minima, index-1 saddles, index-2\n370-    saddles, maxima, and degenerate points.\n371-\n372:EmbedVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n373-                          color_scheme=[\"#9d2c00\", \"#f0c571\", \"#0b81a2\",\n374-                                        \"#e25759\", \"#7e4794\", \"#59a89c\"])\n375-    Displays vector critical points as spheres. The six colors represent sources,\n376-    saddles, sinks, source spirals, centers, and sink spirals.\n377-\n378:EmbedSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n379-                                     color_scheme=[\"#ffffff\", \"#ff8cc6\"])\n380-    Displays symmetric-tensor degenerate points. The two colors represent\n381-    trisectors and wedges; radius controls sphere size.\n382-\n383:EmbedAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n384-                                      color_scheme=[\"#ffffff\", \"#ff8cc6\"])\n385-    Displays asymmetric-tensor degenerate points. The two colors represent\n386-    trisectors and wedges; radius controls sphere size.\n--\n389-POINT TRACKING AND TRACKED-POINT EMBEDDING\n390-------------------------------------------\n391-\n392:Tracking requires a time-series root. For each Track... node, time_steps is a\n393-positive number of steps or -1 for every available step. backend must be \"emd\",\n394-\"sinkhorn\", or \"partial\".\n395-\n396:TrackScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, time_steps, backend)\n397:    Tracks scalar critical points over time.\n398-\n399:TrackVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, time_steps, backend)\n400:    Tracks vector critical points over time.\n401-\n402:TrackSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, time_steps, backend)\n403:    Tracks symmetric-tensor degenerate points over time.\n404-\n405:TrackAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, time_steps, backend)\n406:    Tracks asymmetric-tensor degenerate points over time.\n407-\n408:EmbedTrackedScalarFieldCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0)\n409-    Displays tracked scalar critical points, colored by tracked identity. radius\n410-    controls sphere size.\n411-\n412:EmbedTrackedVectorFieldCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0)\n413-    Displays tracked vector critical points, colored by tracked identity.\n414-\n415:EmbedTrackedSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0)\n416-    Displays tracked symmetric-tensor degenerate points, colored by identity.\n417-\n418:EmbedTrackedAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0)\n419-    Displays tracked asymmetric-tensor degenerate points, colored by identity.\n420-\n421-\n--\n426-\n427-    scalar = LoadScalarField(load_path, \"pressure\")\n428-    simplified = PersistenceSimplification(scalar.id, 0.05)\n429:    field_view = EmbedScalarField(simplified.id, \"viridis\")\n430-    pd = ComputePersistenceDiagram(simplified.id)\n431:    pd_view = EmbedPersistenceDiagram(pd.id)\n432-    nodes_to_visualize = [field_view, pd_view]\n433-\n434:Vector magnitude displayed as a scalar:\n435-\n436:    vector = LoadVectorField(load_path, \"u\", \"v\")\n437:    magnitude = VectorFieldMagnitude(vector.id)\n438:    magnitude_view = EmbedScalarField(magnitude.id, \"inferno\")\n439-\n440:Tracked scalar critical points:\n441-\n442-    scalar = LoadScalarField(load_path, \"pressure\")\n443:    critical = ComputeScalarCriticalPoints(scalar.id, \"maxima\")\n444:    tracked = TrackScalarCriticalPoints(critical.id, -1, \"sinkhorn\")\n445:    tracked_view = EmbedTrackedScalarFieldCriticalPoints(tracked.id, radius=3.0)\n446-\n447-Asymmetric-tensor eigenvalue partition:\n448-\n449-    tensor = LoadAsymmetricTensorField(load_path, \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\")\n450:    partition_view = EmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvaluePartition(\n451-        tensor.id,\n452-        resolution=32,\n453-    )\n--\n460-  2. Implement pipeline(load_path).\n461-  3. Begin each branch with the correct loader and exact VTI array names.\n462-  4. Pass parent.id into every child node and keep node types compatible.\n463:  5. End every displayed branch with an Embed... node.\n464-  6. Return the four required pipeline values.\n465-  7. Implement create_view() and return the RenderView.\n466-  8. Test one time step to PNG before rendering an entire MP4.\nfrom paraview.simple import *\nfrom topopilot.nodes import *\nimport topopilot.config as config\nimport topopilot.nodeTree as tree\nimport argparse\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nDEFAULT_RANDOM_SEED = 0\n\ndef pipeline(load_path):\n    pass\n\ndef create_view():\n    pass\n\ndef validate_arguments(args):\n    if args.i[-4:] == \".vti\":\n        time_steps = 1\n    else:\n        if not os.path.isdir(args.i):\n            print(\"error: file specified with -i must either be .vti file or directory\")\n            exit(1)\n        \n        time_steps = len(os.listdir(args.i))\n        \n        basename = os.path.basename(args.i)\n        dirname = os.path.dirname(args.i)\n\n        for i in range(1,time_steps+1):\n            \n            if not os.path.isfile(f\"{dirname}/{basename}/{basename}{i}.vti\"):\n                print(\"error: invalid input format for directory\")\n                print(f\"missing file {dirname}/{basename}/{basename}{i}.vti\")\n                exit(1)\n        \n    if args.t > time_steps:\n        print(\"error: time step is too high\")\n        exit(1)                             \n\n    if args.x and args.t == -1 and time_steps > 1:\n        print(\"error: cannot run interactive mode on multiple time steps\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.o != \"\" and args.x:\n        print(\"error: you cannot specify an output file and -interactive\")\n        exit(1)\n    \n    if args.o == \"\" and not args.x:\n        print(\"error: you must either specify an output file or run in interactive mode.\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.t == -1 and time_steps > 1 and args.o[-4:] != \".mp4\":\n        print(\"error: when outputting to video format your output filename must end in .mp4\")\n        exit(1)\n    \n    if args.t != -1 and not args.x and args.o[-4:] != \".png\":\n        print(\"error: when outputting to image format your output filename must end in .png\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.t == -1 and time_steps == 1:\n        args.t = 1\n\n    return time_steps\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"User generated scientific visualization pipeline. Generates images or videos based on user input.\")\n\n    parser.add_argument(\"-i\", help=\"The file that should be loaded.\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-x\", help=\"Should you load into interactive mode? (no images will be generated)\", action=argparse.BooleanOptionalAction)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-o\", help=\"The name of the file that we are outputting.\", default=\"\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"-t\", help=\"What time step should be loaded. Put -1 to generate a video of all time steps. If the data only has one time step, -1 will just load the one time step.\", type=int, default=-1)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-q\", help=\"What folder should be used for temporary files\", default=\".\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--seed\", help=\"Seed for TopoPilot-owned random colors and identifiers.\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_RANDOM_SEED)\n\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    time_steps = validate_arguments(args)\n\n    config.set_random_seed(args.seed)\n    config.change_session_folder(args.q)\n\n    sessionDir = Path(f\"{config.session_folder()}\")\n    sessionDir.mkdir(exist_ok = True)\n    cacheDir = Path(f\"{config.session_folder()}/cache\")\n    cacheDir.mkdir(exist_ok = True)\n\n    nodes_to_visualize, color_bar_info, time_invariant_nodes_to_cache, normal_nodoes_to_cache = pipeline(args.i)\n\n    if args.t != -1:\n\n        renderView = create_view()\n        renderView.Background = [1.0, 1.0, 1.0]\n        renderView.UseColorPaletteForBackground = 0\n\n        for n in nodes_to_visualize:\n            props = n.visualize(args.t, renderView)\n\n            if n.id in color_bar_info:\n                position, length, title = color_bar_info[n.id]\n\n                lut = props.LookupTable\n                bar = GetScalarBar(lut, renderView)\n\n                bar.WindowLocation = \"Any Location\"\n                bar.Position = position\n                bar.ScalarBarLength = length\n                bar.Title = title\n                bar.ComponentTitle = ''\n\n                props.SetScalarBarVisibility(renderView, True)\n\n        if args.o:\n            SaveScreenshot(args.o)\n        else:\n            Interact()\n\n    else:\n\n        for t in range(time_steps):\n\n            renderView = create_view()\n\n            for n in nodes_to_visualize:\n                props = n.visualize(t+1, renderView)\n\n                if n.id in color_bar_info:\n                    position, length, title = color_bar_info[n.id]\n\n                    lut = props.LookupTable\n                    bar = GetScalarBar(lut, renderView)\n\n                    bar.WindowLocation = \"Any Location\"\n                    bar.Position = position\n                    bar.ScalarBarLength = length\n                    bar.Title = title\n                    bar.ComponentTitle = ''\n\n                    props.SetScalarBarVisibility(renderView, True)\n\n            SaveScreenshot(f\"{args.q}/frame{str(t+1).zfill(8)}.png\", renderView)\n\n            Disconnect()\n            tree.clear_evaluation_cache()\n            Connect()\n\n        os.system(f\"ffmpeg -framerate 4 -i {args.q}/frame%08d.png -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p {args.o}\")\n\n        for t in range(time_steps):\n            os.remove(f\"{args.q}/frame{str(t+1).zfill(8)}.png\")\nfrom paraview.simple import *\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .node import Guardrail, Node, ModuleSummary, raise_on_tool_param_false\n\nfrom topopilot.utils import is_2d, paraview_vti_to_numpy, numpy_to_paraview_vti\nfrom topopilot.types import Scalar, Vector, SymmetricTensor, AsymmetricTensor, SurfaceOrVolumeEmbedding, \\\n                            EigenvectorPartitionEmbedding, EigenvaluePartitionEmbedding\nfrom topopilot.types.nodeData import SquareOrCubeEmbedding\nfrom topopilot.resources.colormaps import colormaps\nfrom topopilot.mcp_tools.options import options_lists, enumerate_list\nimport topopilot.nodeTree as tree\nfrom topopilot.config import correctness_checks_on\nfrom ..api.prompts import get_prompt\n\nfrom topopilot._topopilot_cpp import lic, eigenvector_partition, eigenvalue_partition\n\n_visualize_alongside_descriptors_guardrail = Guardrail(\n    get_prompt(\"guardrails\", \"fields_with_descriptors\"),\n    \"field_visualized_alongside_descriptors\",\n    \"Set to True if this field is visualized alongside with anything derived from it that the user wants to visualize.\",\n    raise_on_tool_param_false(\"Cannot create this node because the this field should be visualized in the same \"\\\n                              \"visualization as something derived from it that the user wants to visualize.\")\n)\n\nclass EmbedScalarField(Node):\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str, colormap : str = \"cool warm\"):\n\n        if correctness_checks_on():\n            if colormap not in options_lists[\"colormaps\"]:\n                raise Exception(f\"Colormap for EmbedScalarField must match one of the valid options ({enumerate_list(colormaps)})\")\n\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, Scalar, SurfaceOrVolumeEmbedding, locals(), True, True)\n        self.colormap = colormap\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued embedding scalar field\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        from topopilot.config import correctness_checks_on\n        desc = 'Creates a geometric embedding of a node of type scalar. '\n\n        if correctness_checks_on():\n            desc += 'Make sure to use this on the un-simplified scalar field '\\\n                    'unless the user says otherwise (if they say nothing, assume they want the un-simplified one)'\n\n        return desc\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {'parent_node_id': 'The node corresponding to the scalar field that is being visualized.',\n         'colormap': 'The colormap used for the visualization. Select one from '\n                     'OPTIONS:colormaps.'}\n\n    def compatible_to_visualize(self, other):\n        if issubclass(other.node_type, SquareOrCubeEmbedding):\n            return False, f\"Cannot embed a node of type {self.node_type.get_mcp_name()} along with another \"\\\n                          f\"of type {other.node_type.get_mcp_name()}. They will overlap in the visualization\"\n\n        return True, \"\"\n\n    def _evaluation_logic(self, parent_data, time_step):\n        sf = servermanager.Fetch(parent_data[0].data)\n        dimensions = self.root_node.dimensions\n\n        opacity_tf = None\n\n        if not is_2d(dimensions):\n\n            opacity_tf = []\n\n            numPoints = sf.GetNumberOfPoints()\n            skip = int(numPoints/1000000)\n            if skip == 0:\n                skip = 1\n            array = sf.GetPointData().GetArray(\"Scalars_\")\n\n            values = []\n            \n            for i in range(0, numPoints, skip):\n                values.append(array.GetTuple1(i))\n            numPoints = len(values)\n            values.sort()\n\n            window_size = int(0.2*numPoints)\n\n            greatest_window = None\n            greatest_window_range = -float('inf')\n            \n            for i in range(1,numPoints-window_size):\n                window_range = values[i+window_size] - values[i]\n                if window_range > greatest_window_range:\n                    greatest_window = i\n                    greatest_window_range = window_range\n\n            # rename for ease of writing\n            w = values[greatest_window]\n            r = greatest_window_range\n\n            opacity_tf.append((w, 0.0))\n            opacity_tf.append((w + 0.25*r, 0.2))\n            opacity_tf.append((w + 0.375*r, 0.5))\n            opacity_tf.append((w + 0.5*r, 1.0))\n            opacity_tf.append((w + 0.625*r, 0.5))\n            opacity_tf.append((w + 0.75*r, 0.2))\n            opacity_tf.append((w + r, 0.0))\n\n        return SurfaceOrVolumeEmbedding(parent_data[time_step-1].data, self.colormap, opacity_tf, dimensions, False, True)\n\n    def _evaluation_logic_partial_cache(self, parent_data, partial_cache, time_step):\n        partial_cache.data = parent_data.data\n        return partial_cache\n    \n    @classmethod\n    def guardrails(cls):\n        def guardrail_function(parent_node_id, colormap):\n            if tree.has_node(parent_node_id) and type(tree.node(parent_node_id)).__name__ == \"PersistenceSimplification\":\n                raise Exception(\"Error: You are creating a visualization of a simplified scalar field, however the user did not \"\n                                \"explicitly ask for the simplified scalar field to be visualized. Unless the user says otherwise, you\" \\\n                                \"should assume that the unsimplified scalar field should be visualized.\")\n\n        return [\n            Guardrail(\n                \"Unless the user explicitly says otherwise, this should be used to visualize the un-simplified scalar field.\",\n                \"user_allowed_visualizing_simplified_scalar_field\",\n                \"Set to True if the explicitly clarified that they want the simplified scalar field to be visualized.\",\n                guardrail_function\n            ),\n            _visualize_alongside_descriptors_guardrail\n        ]\n\nclass EmbedVectorField(Node):\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str):\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, Vector, SurfaceOrVolumeEmbedding, locals())\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued embedding vector field\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        return 'Creates a geometric embedding of a node of type vector.'\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {'parent_node_id': 'The id of a node of type vector that should be embedded'}\n\n    @classmethod\n    def guardrails(cls):\n        return [_visualize_alongside_descriptors_guardrail]\n\n    def compatible_to_visualize(self, other):\n        if issubclass(other.node_type, SquareOrCubeEmbedding):\n            return False, f\"Cannot embed a node of type {self.node_type.get_mcp_name()} along with another \"\\\n                          f\"of type {other.node_type.get_mcp_name()}. They will overlap in the visualization\"\n\n        return True, \"\"\n\n    def _evaluation_logic(self, parent_data, time_step):\n        array = paraview_vti_to_numpy(parent_data.data)\n        lic_array = lic(array, 4)\n        data = numpy_to_paraview_vti(lic_array, 4)\n\n        return SurfaceOrVolumeEmbedding(data, \"grey\", None, array.shape)\n\nclass EmbedSymmetricTensorField(Node):\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str):\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, SymmetricTensor, SurfaceOrVolumeEmbedding, locals())\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued embedding symmetric tensor field\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        return 'Creates a geometric embedding of a node of type symmetric_tensor.'\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {'parent_node_id': 'The id of a node of type symmetric_tensor that should be embedded'}\n\n    @classmethod\n    def guardrails(cls):\n        return [_visualize_alongside_descriptors_guardrail]\n\n    def compatible_to_visualize(self, other):\n        if issubclass(other.node_type, SquareOrCubeEmbedding):\n            return False, f\"Cannot embed a node of type {self.node_type.get_mcp_name()} along with another \"\\\n                          f\"of type {other.node_type.get_mcp_name()}. They will overlap in the visualization\"\n\n        return True, \"\"\n\n    def _evaluation_logic(self, parent_data, time_step):\n        resolution = 16\n\n        array = paraview_vti_to_numpy(parent_data.data)\n        lic_array = lic(array, 16)\n        data = numpy_to_paraview_vti(lic_array, 16)\n\n        return SurfaceOrVolumeEmbedding(data, \"grey\", None, array.shape)\n\nclass EmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvectorPartition(Node):\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str, resolution : int = 16):\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, AsymmetricTensor, EigenvectorPartitionEmbedding, locals())\n\n        self.resolution = resolution\n\n    @classmethod\n    def guardrails(cls):\n        return [\n            Guardrail(\n                get_prompt(\"guardrails\", \"eigenvector_partition_degenerate_points\"),\n                \"degenerate_points_are_also_embedded\",\n                \"Set to True if degenerate points will be separately computed and visualized. Set to False otherwise.\",\n                raise_on_tool_param_false(\n                    \"Cannot create this node because visualizing the eigenvector partition also requires separately \"\n                    \"computing and visualizing the degenerate points.\"\n                ),\n            ),\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
